--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,6 +41,19 @@ RelayBoard is a small job-control application with:
 
 The implementation should remain small enough that a reviewer can inspect the whole system.
 
+## Pause and resume
+
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/pause` and `POST /api/jobs/{id}/resume` accept no
+required body and return HTTP 200 with the updated `job` object. Repeated calls
+are idempotent; unknown jobs return HTTP 404. Job objects include `paused`.
+
+Pause prevents new scheduled Runs (HTTP 409) while allowing manual Runs and
+existing Runs, retries, and alerts to continue normally. Pause is persisted
+independently of `enabled`: resume clears pause but does not enable a disabled
+Job or start a Run. The dashboard shows pause separately from enabled and keeps
+the last completed Run result. Existing databases acquire an unpaused default
+when opened.
+
 ## Treatment isolation
 
 Treatment agents receive the fixture workspace and scenario prompt.
